      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated NbMoTaW has very poor room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The irradiation response of NbMoTaW has only been inferred computationally.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chromium is a ductility-promoting addition for NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5 at.% Cr and applying a controlled post-casting heat treatment will generate nanoscale B2 or FCC-like precipitates in the BCC NbMoTaW matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10154406::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The induced second-phase precipitates will be ductile.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoscale precipitates will act as irradiation-defect sinks.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates will provide compatible additional slip systems and thereby increase room-temperature plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fine precipitate dispersion will enhance defect recombination and self-healing under irradiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-modified and heat-treated alloy will have significantly greater room-temperature ductility than untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr-modified alloy will show improved irradiation tolerance, including fewer or smaller helium bubbles, relative to untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10154406::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modification will reduce helium-induced blistering and irradiation-induced amorphization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dominant BCC matrix will retain its high-temperature strength and phase stability up to approximately 1600 °C after Cr addition and precipitation heat treatment.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The response at extreme irradiation fluences and after long-duration exposure remains unvalidated.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of the ductility and irradiation-tolerance improvements and the stability of the precipitates under combined heat and irradiation are uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
